/*
 * TestArm64SemanticsSme.cpp
 *
 * Tests of the A64 SME and SME2 lifter (Arm64SemanticSme.h): the instructions run by the
 * interpreter against the values of an independent model of the Arm ARM pseudocode (the rows
 * of tests/arm/Arm64SmeSemanticRows.inc, generated by tests/arm/tools/gen_sme_semantic_rows.py
 * with tests/arm/tools/sme_model.py), the instructions outside of their mode, and the
 * streaming mode / za transitions of smstart, smstop and msr svcr.
 *
 * The differential tests against the Apple M4 (tests/arm/semantics, corpus a64_sme*.s) cover
 * the instructions it implements (FEAT_SME, SME2, SME_F64F64, SME_I16I64); these rows cover
 * the others (the half precision and BFloat16 arithmetic of FEAT_SME_F16F16 and
 * FEAT_SME_B16B16, FAMINMAX, SVE BFSCALE, SME2.1 movaz, SME2.2 fmul, the scalar movt) and pin
 * the rest.
 *
 * Author: Elad Raz <e@eladraz.com>
 */
